  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on outcomes with less than 20% probability, upweighting them. In this case, the 20% outcome in B is not below the threshold, so technically no adjustment applies. However, the individual is focusing on the same outcome — the 20% chance of 0€ — and evaluating its importance in the decision. While the verbal report shows attention to the low-probability favorable outcome in B, consistent with the informational focus of the reason, the reason's specific rule (upweighting <20% outcomes) does not apply here because the probability is exactly 20%. The individual does not mention any adjustment of probabilities or systematic weighting; they are instead making a qualitative trade-off judgment. Thus, while the individual considers the same type of information (the small-probability favorable outcome), they do not appear to apply the specific rule of the decision reason (adjusted probability weighting). The consideration is similar in spirit but not in mechanism. Therefore, it is unlikely the exact reason was used, though related thinking is present.",
  "final_assessment_score": 30
