  "step_3": "The decision reason requires focusing on outcomes with probabilities below 20% and up-weighting them, but neither lottery contains such outcomes (both are at or above 20%). Therefore, the mechanism of the decision reason is inactive in this case. The individual does not refer to any adjustment of probabilities or special attention to rare events. Instead, the justification centers on loss magnitude and affective reaction, not on probability transformation. There is no evidence that the individual considered weighting low-probability outcomes more heavily, nor did they engage in the type of calculation or reasoning the decision reason prescribes. The reasoning process described is inconsistent with the decision reason’s rule, even if the final choice aligns with it.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
