  "step_2": "The individual reports a desire to win something positive after previous risk-seeking rounds. They state that Lottery B was chosen because the probability of winning something (i.e., non-zero outcome) is higher in B than in A. In Lottery A, the chance of a non-zero outcome is 25% (only 6000 Euros). In Lottery B, the chance of a non-zero outcome is 50% (25% for 4000 and 25% for 2000). The individual acknowledges that the potential winnings in B are lower than in A but prioritizes the higher chance of gaining something over the amount. The justification centers on the psychological desire to experience a positive outcome and the higher probability of any gain in B, not on specific outcome-probability weighting or numerical calculations involving small probabilities.",
